Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/MediaCodec.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0060 e2b3: the static initializer loads no libmedia_jni, and a tunneled session's audio sync is the invalid one.

Why: Android's MediaCodec natives live in libmedia_jni, which Minato does not build; they are libandroid_runtime's
(framework/native/android_runtime/android_media_MediaCodec.cpp), registered when the process starts, so the load would
throw UnsatisfiedLinkError out of <clinit>. native_init stays. The audio session's hardware sync for tunneled playback
(setParameters' and configure's KEY_AUDIO_SESSION_ID) is AudioSystem's, a compile-only stub here: Minato's audio has
no hardware sync, so it is AUDIO_HW_SYNC_INVALID (0), what Android's AudioSystem answers for a session without one
[inferred: AudioSystem.java's AUDIO_HW_SYNC_INVALID].

--- a/media/java/android/media/MediaCodec.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/MediaCodec.java
@@ -2395,7 +2395,7 @@
                         throw new IllegalArgumentException("Wrong Session ID Parameter!");
                     }
                     keys[i] = "audio-hw-sync";
-                    values[i] = AudioSystem.getAudioHwSyncForSession(sessionId);
+                    values[i] = 0 /* Minato: AudioSystem.AUDIO_HW_SYNC_INVALID, no hardware sync */;
                 } else {
                     keys[i] = entry.getKey();
                     values[i] = entry.getValue();
@@ -5214,7 +5214,7 @@
                     throw new IllegalArgumentException("Wrong Session ID Parameter!");
                 }
                 keys[i] = "audio-hw-sync";
-                values[i] = AudioSystem.getAudioHwSyncForSession(sessionId);
+                values[i] = 0 /* Minato: AudioSystem.AUDIO_HW_SYNC_INVALID, no hardware sync */;
             } else {
                 keys[i] = key;
                 Object value = params.get(key);
@@ -5756,7 +5756,7 @@
     private native final void native_finalize();
 
     static {
-        System.loadLibrary("media_jni");
+        // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's (android_media_MediaCodec.cpp), registered at the start.
         native_init();
     }
 
